  "reason": "The records collectively disclose the essential processing strategy and strengthening rationale. R4 and R14 show high-energy mechanical alloying of equiatomic elemental powders under argon to form nonequilibrium solid solutions, while R5, R7, R11, R12, R15, R16, and R20 establish subsequent SPS consolidation of mechanically alloyed HEA powders. R5 directly connects longer milling, severe plastic deformation, finer bulk grains, Hall–Petch strengthening, and hardness near 676 HV; R9 and R11 add solid-solution and grain-boundary strengthening, and R6 links severe deformation, defect accumulation, refinement, and FCC/BCC phase evolution in the closely related AlCoCrFeNi system. Thus an expert could plausibly propose short-duration HEBM followed by rapid SPS for CoCrFeNiTi and predict high hardness and strength from grain refinement, defects, and solid-solution effects. The exact 900–1000 °C window, 83/17 FCC/BCC ratio, and precise role assigned to Ti are not directly disclosed, but they are system-specific optimization rather than a substantial new processing or mechanistic idea."
